    {
      "title": "Trump names Katie Zacharia as White House press secy, replacing Leavitt",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/trump-names-katie-zacharia-as-white-house-press-secy-replacing-leavitt-126101000066_1.html",
      "description": "US President Donald Trump announced Friday that Katie Zacharia, a communications adviser for his media company, will succeed Karoline Leavitt as White House press secretary.\nTrump revealed his selection of Zacharia on his Truth Social platform, where he often makes political and official announcements. Zacharia is a conservative commentator for Trump Media & Technology Group, which operates the social media site.\nIn naming Zacharia, Trump described her as \"a loyal and brilliant supporter, right from the beginning.\"\nZacharia briefly worked as a spokesperson for the Department of Homeland Security earlier this year and has been a commentator for Fox News and Newsmax. Trump said Zacharia had been involved in his presidential campaigns, notably in swing states.\nA request for comment left with Zacharia was not immediately answered. A LinkedIn profile noted that she earned a law degree from Pepperdine University.\nLeavitt announced her departure Aug. 12 and left the position Aug. 27.\nSh",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-10T02:46:26"
    }
